Testing and Troubleshooting

I tested the website locally using Python's HTTP server and Chrome Developer Tools.

Testing included:
Verifying that the website loaded successfully.
Testing the interactive courtroom features.
Checking the website's responsive layout.
Reviewing the browser console for errors.

Favicon Error
The browser console displayed an HTTP 404 error because the website did not contain a favicon.

I resolved this by adding the following HTML to the <head> section of index.html:
<link rel="icon" href="data:,">
This prevented unnecessary favicon requests.

Deployment
I initialized a local Git repository, committed the project files, and pushed them to GitHub.
I then configured GitHub Pages to publish the website from the main branch.
I reviewed the website's functionality, tested its interactive features,
and configured the project for deployment using GitHub Pages.

